# The TAUxx variants are ZERO when the super-layer is clear. These are the
# HISTORICAL exports, but are non-ideal as *in-cloud* diagnostics. The
# COTxx are to be prefered.
 TAULO     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_low_clouds                               
 TAUMD     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_middle_clouds                            
 TAUHI     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_high_clouds                              
 TAUTT     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_all_clouds__deprecated                   
 TAUTX     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_all_clouds                               
# The COTxx variants are UNDEF when the super-layer is clear. They are
# preferred over TAUxx.
 COTLO     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_low_clouds_clrundef                      
 COTMD     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_middle_clouds_clrundef                   
 COTHI     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_high_clouds_clrundef                     
 COTTT     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_all_clouds_clrundef                      
# COT[DEN|NUM]xx allow a true cloud-fraction-weighted in-cloud optical
# thickness to be calculated via COTNUMxx / COTDENxx. Like the COTxx, clear
# values make no contribution, but unlike COTxx, each COT is weighted by a
# cloud fraction so that small clouds, which have a small radiative effect,
# get weighted accordingly. These provide the best estimate of radiatively
# effective in-cloud optical thicknesses, but require more advance post-
# processing (summing both NUM and DEN fields over the time-period required,
# and only then taking their quotient.)
 COTDENLO  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_low_clouds_denominator                   
 COTDENMD  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_middle_clouds_denominator                
 COTDENHI  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_high_clouds_denominator                  
 COTDENTT  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_all_clouds_denominator                   
 COTNUMLO  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_low_clouds_numerator                     
 COTNUMMD  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_middle_clouds_numerator                  
 COTNUMHI  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_high_clouds_numerator                    
 COTNUMTT  | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | in_cloud_optical_thickness_of_all_clouds_numerator                     
