# COSZ is instantaneous at the end of the UPDATE period, so it is
# consistent with the HISTORY files output time. MCOSZ is the mean over the
# update period, so it will be half a heartbeat behind the HISTORY file
# time, but is the flux-weighted and update-interval-averaged COSZ value
# used by the UPDATE. (Also see COSZSW under INTERNAL, above, for a third.)
 COSZ      | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | cosine_of_the_solar_zenith_angle                                       
 MCOSZ     | 1     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | mean_cosine_of_the_solar_zenith_angle                                  
 CLDTMP    | K     | xy   | N    |                       |                  | cloud_top_temperature                                                  
 CLDPRS    | Pa    | xy   | N    |                       |                  | cloud_top_pressure                                                     
# The four CLDxxSWHB diagnostics represent super-layer cloud fractions based
# on essentially the same subcolumn cloud generation used by RRTMG SW but
# called from within the SOLAR UPDATE at the HEARTBEAT. They are GLOBAL (not
# just sunlit) fields and generated on the heartbeat. BUT, because subcolumn
# cloud generation is EXPENSIVE, asking for any of these exports will DOUBLE
# the cost of running the SOLAR GC. As such, they are for SPECIAL VALIDATION
# PURPOSES ONLY. No cost is incurred if they are not exported. But we gate
# them with USE_SOLAR_RADVAL as an extra protection against their
# inadvertant use. Note, also, that they are NOT EXACTLY heartbeat versions
# of CLDxxSW, since they sample the heartbeat cloud fractions, not the less
# frequent snapshots used at REFRESH-frequency, and also since the
# generation inside UPDATE is on non-flipped vertical fields. This latter
# difference should be statistically insignificant. A re-coding to use
# vertically flipped fields as per RRTMG SW is possible but will be
# slightly slower, and was deemed unnecessary since the cloud fraction
# frequency difference will likely dominate.
 CLDTTSWHB | 1     | xy   | N    |                       | USE_SOLAR_RADVAL | total_cloud_area_fraction_rrtmg_sw_HEARTBEAT                           
 CLDHISWHB | 1     | xy   | N    |                       | USE_SOLAR_RADVAL | high-level_cloud_area_fraction_rrtmg_sw_HEARTBEAT                      
 CLDMDSWHB | 1     | xy   | N    |                       | USE_SOLAR_RADVAL | mid-level_cloud_area_fraction_rrtmg_sw_HEARTBEAT                       
 CLDLOSWHB | 1     | xy   | N    |                       | USE_SOLAR_RADVAL | low-level_cloud_area_fraction_rrtmg_sw_HEARTBEAT                       

